# Goal seek

solve(constraint) makes the definition's own name the unknown and finds the
boundary value through any chain of calculations.

[$1,200]:saved
[9]:months_left
[saved_by_june] := monthly * months_left + saved
[monthly] := solve(saved_by_june >= $5,000)

Save [monthly] a month to reach [saved_by_june] by June.

[30m]:per_call
[calls] := solve(calls * per_call <= 4h)

That is [calls] calls in an afternoon.

<!-- Hover monthly to see which side of the boundary it sits on. -->
